    question: 'What are the components of a ventilator care bundle to prevent VAE/VAP?',
    answer: 'Evidence-based ventilator bundle components include: (1) Elevation of the head of bed to 30-45 degrees to reduce aspiration risk. (2) Daily sedation interruption (SAT) and assessment of readiness for extubation (SBT). (3) Peptic ulcer disease prophylaxis (H2 blockers or PPIs for high-risk patients). (4) Deep venous thrombosis prophylaxis (pharmacologic or mechanical). (5) Daily oral care with chlorhexidine (though recent evidence has questioned mortality benefit). (6) Subglottic suctioning using specially designed ETTs. (7) Maintaining ETT cuff pressure at 20-30 cmH2O. (8) Minimizing circuit breaks and changes. (9) Early mobilization. Bundle compliance is tracked as an all-or-none measure, and high compliance rates (greater than 95%) are associated with significant VAP/VAE reduction.',
