    question: 'What is the role of checklists in ICU safety, and what evidence supports their use?',
    answer: 'ICU checklists ensure consistent completion of evidence-based practices by reducing reliance on memory and creating a shared mental model. Evidence includes the landmark Pronovost study showing a central line insertion checklist reduced catheter-related bloodstream infections by 66% (from 11.5 to 0 per 1,000 catheter-days). Daily goals checklists improve communication and reduce ICU length of stay. Surgical safety checklists (WHO Surgical Safety Checklist) reduce surgical complications by 36% and mortality by 47%. Effective checklists share features: they are concise, focus on critical steps with potential for error, include a verification pause (hard stop), empower any team member to halt the process, and are integrated into workflow rather than being add-ons. Barriers include checklist fatigue and superficial compliance without genuine engagement.',
