    answer: 'Early mobility protocols progressively advance patients from passive range of motion to sitting, standing, and ambulation while still on mechanical ventilation or vasoactive support. Benefits include reduced ICU-acquired weakness, shorter delirium duration, improved functional status at discharge, shorter ventilator days and ICU stay, and reduced mortality. Safety screening criteria before mobilization include: hemodynamic stability (no active titration of vasopressors, MAP greater than 65), adequate oxygenation (SpO2 greater than 88% on FiO2 less than 0.6), no active hemorrhage or unstable fractures, no evidence of elevated intracranial pressure, no active myocardial ischemia, secure airway with adequate ETT cuff pressure, and no femoral vascular access devices that preclude hip flexion. Activity is stopped for new arrhythmias, desaturation, hypotension, or patient distress.',
