    divisionId: ACCS_DIVISION_ID,
    question: 'What is the systematic approach to refractory hypoxemia in a mechanically ventilated patient?',
    answer: 'A stepwise algorithm for refractory hypoxemia includes: (1) Verify the basics: confirm ETT position, rule out right mainstem intubation, check for circuit disconnect or leak, ensure adequate FiO2 delivery. (2) Optimize conventional ventilation: increase PEEP using a PEEP-FiO2 table or best compliance strategy, ensure adequate tidal volume delivery, perform recruitment maneuvers. (3) Positioning: prone positioning for at least 16 hours in severe ARDS. (4) Neuromuscular blockade: cisatracurium for 48 hours to improve chest wall compliance and reduce oxygen consumption. (5) Inhaled vasodilators: inhaled nitric oxide or inhaled epoprostenol to improve V/Q matching. (6) Alternative ventilator modes: APRV or high-frequency oscillatory ventilation. (7) Extracorporeal support: VV-ECMO when PaO2/FiO2 remains less than 80 despite optimization. Each step is evaluated before escalating to the next.',
