    divisionId: ACCS_DIVISION_ID,
    question: 'A ventilated ARDS patient on PEEP 14, FiO2 0.80, with P/F ratio of 85, suddenly develops subcutaneous emphysema, hypotension, and absent breath sounds on the right. SpO2 drops to 78%. What is the diagnosis and what should the respiratory therapist do immediately?',
