    question: 'A 72-year-old with COPD on BiPAP presents with worsening ABG: pH 7.22, PaCO2 88 mmHg, PaO2 52 mmHg, HCO3 34 mEq/L. BiPAP settings are IPAP 18/EPAP 8. What does the ABG reveal, and what adjustments should be made before considering intubation?',
